# =============================================================================
#  .dockerignore - what NOT to send to the Docker daemon
# =============================================================================
#  Everything not listed here becomes part of the BUILD CONTEXT, which is copied
#  to the Docker daemon before the build even starts. Without this file the
#  context includes bin/, obj/ and .git/ - often hundreds of megabytes - which
#  makes every build slow AND can bake stale, host-built binaries into the image.
#
#  SECURITY ANGLE: it also stops secrets (.env, *.pfx, user secrets) from being
#  copied into a layer. Deleting a file in a LATER layer does not remove it from
#  the image - anyone can still extract it from the earlier layer.
# =============================================================================

# Build output - the image builds its own; host binaries may target another OS.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/

# Version control
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes

# IDE / editor
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.DotSettings

# Docker files themselves (not needed inside the image)
**/Dockerfile*
**/docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Secrets and local environment - MUST never enter an image
**/*.env
.env
**/secrets.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12

# Docs and scratch files
**/*.md
docs/
guide/
LICENSE

# macOS / Windows noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
